# QA M7 acceptance, BUG (E51 / D-106 as-built "where the hit labels hang"):
# the boss's hit labels cover Resi when she steps off a refuge onto his
# head and drifts to the room side. E51 promises the labels "start below
# her as she bounces off and never cover her". That holds for a high
# bounce straight back (the solver's hits from the counter), but a step-off
# with the direction still held is a low bounce (vy -900) that carries her
# 20-40 px towards the room, exactly into the label column (42 px from his
# centre), and she falls back down through it.
# Steps: the solver's route to the counter (frames 0-1234, cafe_zauner_solver
# unchanged), stand on the counter while he telegraphs and dashes right
# (breather at the counter from 1272), walk left off the counter's edge
# (LEFT 14 frames from 1272) onto his head: hit 1 at 1297, 1000 +
# „Unerhört!". With nothing held she drifts left and falls past him.
# Expected: no frame where „Unerhört!" or its „1000" is drawn over Resi.
# Actual: frames 1314-1325 the label pair is drawn over her whole body
# (text x 201-243 / 210-234 on screen, Resi x 219-241, y 87-147); at 1318-
# 1320 only her hair and skirt show between the two lines. The same
# happens at the left wall in the documented "forgiving pattern" of the
# Normal win (cafe_zauner_boss_win_normal 1231-1238, 1765-1772, 2243-2250:
# the label's first 3-5 columns over her arm and side as she drops beside
# him), and for every form (a Big/Hackl Resi is 8 px taller).
# Fixed in E53 (D-106 "As built (E53)"): the labels slide ahead of her
# towards the room (or up, or back, never over his face) and never cover
# her. Checked on every frame by xtask's
# `stage_9_popups_never_cover_resi_or_reach_the_hud` (popup_clearance.rs);
# the shots are goldens of the fixed frames (art-director review).
